The potential vulnerability is related to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application processes user-supplied regex patterns without adequate validation or restrictions, allowing an attacker to craft complex regex patterns that can cause excessive backtracking and significantly degrade the performance of the application. If the regex engine is not optimized for handling such patterns, it may lead to high CPU usage or even application crashes, thereby impacting the availability of the service. This type of vulnerability is particularly concerning in APIs that accept regex patterns as input, as it can be exploited by malicious users to disrupt service.

